  "description": "Confirmation that the use of the property as a restaurant with a commercial kitchen and extraction system Use Class (E(b) Sale of food and drink for consumption (mostly) on the premises), for a period of more than 10 years is lawful (Application for a Certificate of Lawful Development for an Existing Use).",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The Local Planning Authority considers that the existing use would fall within a sui generis use class (hot food take-away). As such, the proposal is considered to constitute development as defined by Section 55 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) and the proposed change of use is not one which is permitted by the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended). Furthermore, the proposal would constitute development under Section 55 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended). The proposal therefore requires full planning permission."
